---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AdBreak from "@/components/AdBreak.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Data" description="Source-backed technical reference products from Second Pass.">
  <section class="shell route">
    <header class="route-head">
      <div class="kicker">/ DATA</div>
      <h1>Numbers with their assumptions still attached.</h1>
      <p>
        These are product foundations, not fabricated live datasets. Real values enter only through
        the newsroom's source-backed data workflow. Each product preserves source, date, method, and assumptions.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="data-grid" style="background:var(--rule);border-color:var(--rule)">
      <section id="model-pricing" class="data-module">
        <span class="number">01 / FOUNDATION</span>
        <h3>Model Pricing Index</h3>
        <p>Provider, model/version, input/output/cache pricing, context, effective date, source. Historical pricing with version-level provenance.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="accelerators" class="data-module">
        <span class="number">02 / FOUNDATION</span>
        <h3>Accelerator Index</h3>
        <p>Vendor, SKU, memory, bandwidth, interconnect, power, availability, source. Architecture-level comparison context, not just peak specs.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="benchmarks" class="data-module">
        <span class="number">03 / FOUNDATION</span>
        <h3>Benchmark Registry</h3>
        <p>Metric, workload, hardware, software, precision, test operator, methodology, source. Who ran the test, and under what conditions.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div style="max-width:var(--reading);margin-top:38px;font:1.05rem/1.55 var(--reader);color:var(--graphite)">
      <p>When a data product launches, it will be versioned, sourced, and auditable. No invented production
      data will appear. The newsroom data workflow determines when each product receives real entries.</p>
    </div>

    <AdBreak fallback="data" label="DATA PRODUCT / FUTURE WHOLE-PRODUCT SPONSOR" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
